<h2>Before your first class</h2>
<p>Our Onalaska studio and office are at <strong>923 12th Ave S, Suite 103, Onalaska, WI 54650</strong>. Holmen classes meet inside the <strong>Holmen Boys &amp; Girls Club, 600 Holmen Dr N, Holmen, WI 54636</strong>. Check the location listed for your class when booking. Calls and office inquiries for both locations are handled by our Onalaska team. The Boys &amp; Girls Club has its own operating hours; follow your MDU class schedule for lesson times.</p>
<p>Bring your questions as well as your dancer! Tell us about previous lessons, any worries about trying something new, and what your child enjoys. You can review the dress code and studio policies linked from the <a href="/fall">class schedule</a>, or ask what to wear for a trial before buying dancewear. Check the studio's published dates for breaks when planning your week.</p>
<h2>Make room for dance in your family's routine</h2>
<p>Compare class times with school pickup and other activities, including the return trip home. If you have siblings, ask our team to help compare age groups and available days. For a different seasonal option, explore <a href="/summer">summer classes and camps</a>. For a celebration with friends, see our <a href="/parties">dance birthday parties</a>.</p>
